WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:09.607
"This is so embarrassing," Iris thought as she missed another ball that Jae lobbed her way.

2
00:00:09.608 --> 00:00:14.864
She wished she had paired up with Javier—or anyone else.

3
00:00:14.865 --> 00:00:20.784
"I probably just need to warm up a little," she called to Jae with a nervous laugh.

4
00:00:20.785 --> 00:00:29.051
She exhaled and tried to relax. She took another swing. Another miss.

5
00:00:29.052 --> 00:00:33.775
"Or maybe this racket has a hole in it!" she joked.

6
00:00:33.775 --> 00:00:43.849
"Could be." Jae shrugged and hit another ball to her. Iris swung—and missed again.

7
00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:51.691
Jae scratched his head. "Didn't you say your soccer team made it to the state playoffs?"

8
00:00:51.692 --> 00:01:00.165
"The key word there is soccer ," Iris said. "And trust me, tennis is nothing like

9
00:01:00.166 --> 00:01:07.324
soccer." She looked down and inspected her racket. "Maybe I need a different one of

10
00:01:07.325 --> 00:01:14.895
these." "Having a problem over here?" Trent appeared from behind Iris, making her

11
00:01:14.896 --> 00:01:24.562
jump. "A problem? Uh . . ." Iris didn't know what to say. Instinctively, she glanced over at

12
00:01:24.563 --> 00:01:34.058
Javier. He was swinging his racket like crazy but not coming any closer to hitting the ball than she

13
00:01:34.059 --> 00:01:40.959
was. Trent followed her gaze. "You and Javier have never played tennis before, have

14
00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:50.056
you?" "Nope," Iris said. "Not even table tennis!" She grinned at Jae, and he

15
00:01:50.057 --> 00:01:55.791
chuckled. "It's okay." But Trent was frowning like it really wasn't

16
00:01:55.792 --> 00:02:04.618
okay. "Jae, why don't you partner up with Zoe instead?" He pointed at the blond girl hitting balls at

17
00:02:04.619 --> 00:02:12.182
Javier. Zoe heard Trent and turned to face them. Her face was already lit up into a

18
00:02:12.183 --> 00:02:14.925
smile. "Great idea!" she

19
00:02:14.926 --> 00:02:20.761
called. Jae flashed Zoe a grin. "Sure," he said. "Sounds

20
00:02:20.761 --> 00:02:26.449
good." Iris felt a flush creep up her face. Zoe was very

21
00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:34.347
pretty. Jae seemed very happy to be Zoe's partner, and Zoe looked just as happy to be partners with

22
00:02:34.348 --> 00:02:40.997
him. "You two can start practicing," Trent said to them. Then he waved Javier

23
00:02:40.998 --> 00:02:49.990
over. "I know Julie said we'd figure out the groups after tryouts, but there's no sense in keeping the two of you

24
00:02:49.991 --> 00:02:57.896
here. You really need to learn the basics of tennis first. Besides, the other group has fewer

25
00:02:57.897 --> 00:03:04.149
kids." He pointed to another court, where Ally stood observing the younger

26
00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:12.904
campers. "Just head on over there, and tell Ally I sent you." He turned back to the rest of the older

27
00:03:12.905 --> 00:03:19.054
group. Iris blinked. Trent had just sent them down to the baby

28
00:03:19.055 --> 00:03:24.545
class! She inspected her racket once more before following Javier off the

29
00:03:24.546 --> 00:03:28.204
court. Her brother didn't seem to be bothered in the

30
00:03:28.205 --> 00:03:33.292
slightest. Of course, he wasn't used to excelling at sports like Iris

31
00:03:33.293 --> 00:03:38.455
was. And this was about more than tennis. Jae was

32
00:03:38.456 --> 00:03:47.599
cute. She wanted to be in his group. So Iris had to learn how to play tennis—and learn

33
00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:54.084
fast. Ally saw Iris and Javier approaching. "What's

34
00:03:54.085 --> 00:03:58.852
up?" "Trent sent us to join your group," Iris

35
00:03:58.852 --> 00:04:02.790
mumbled. "We've never played tennis before," Javier

36
00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:06.129
said. "Oh, that's fine," Ally

37
00:04:06.129 --> 00:04:12.427
said. "His group had too many kids anyway, and we can definitely teach you some stuff over

38
00:04:12.428 --> 00:04:16.424
here." She waved at some kids who were playing on the

39
00:04:16.425 --> 00:04:21.167
court. "Grace! Ben! Can you come over here for a

40
00:04:21.168 --> 00:04:35.494
minute?" Grace and Ben each stood about a head shorter than Iris, and their identical blond hair and blue eyes made them seem like polar opposites of Iris and Javier.

41
00:04:35.495 --> 00:04:41.768
"Twins?" All four kids blurted out the word at the same time.

42
00:04:41.769 --> 00:04:48.636
Ally laughed. "Yes! The four of you will be perfect teammates."

43
00:04:48.636 --> 00:04:57.635
Iris smiled as politely as she could, but the idea that these kids were her new teammates was kind of insulting.

44
00:04:57.636 --> 00:05:00.441
They looked about nine years old.

45
00:05:00.442 --> 00:05:04.951
Grace smiled at Iris. "Do you want to come with me?"

46
00:05:04.951 --> 00:05:09.295
Iris shrugged. "I guess," she mumbled.

47
00:05:09.296 --> 00:05:13.376
"So I must be with you," Javier said to Ben.

48
00:05:13.376 --> 00:05:19.213
Iris stared at her brother. He was giving the younger boy a friendly smile.

49
00:05:19.214 --> 00:05:29.186
"Javier seriously doesn't care that we're stuck playing with these little kids!" Iris thought. "Why isn't he embarrassed?"

50
00:05:29.187 --> 00:05:37.025
"Grace and Ben went to our junior camp last year," Ally said. "They won the final match for their age group."

51
00:05:37.026 --> 00:05:41.128
"Wow," Javier said. "Cool."

52
00:05:41.129 --> 00:05:46.265
Iris swallowed. "Great," she thought.

53
00:05:46.265 --> 00:05:53.353
Not only were they stuck with these babies, but these babies actually knew how to play tennis!

54
00:05:53.354 --> 00:05:59.185
Grace led Iris to an empty space on the court.

55
00:05:59.186 --> 00:06:04.317
"You guys must be pretty bad if they sent you down to our group!" she joked.

56
00:06:04.318 --> 00:06:11.340
"We've never played before, that's all," Iris said. "Once I learn what to do, I'll be fine."

57
00:06:11.341 --> 00:06:17.315
"Well, don't worry." Grace smiled. "Ally's a great coach."

58
00:06:17.316 --> 00:06:26.466
Ally jogged over to them. "First things first," she said. "Let me see your swing, Iris."

59
00:06:26.467 --> 00:06:33.240
Iris gripped the racket in both hands and gave it a powerful swing.

60
00:06:33.241 --> 00:06:38.631
"Uh-uh." Grace shook her head. "You're doing it all wrong."

61
00:06:38.631 --> 00:06:40.420
Iris flushed.

62
00:06:40.421 --> 00:06:47.721
"Here, watch me," Ally said. She planted her own feet hip-width apart.

63
00:06:47.721 --> 00:06:54.203
With one hip facing the net, she held her racket gently with both hands.

64
00:06:54.204 --> 00:07:02.617
When she swung, she shifted her weight gracefully toward the net, almost as though she was dancing with her racket.

65
00:07:02.618 --> 00:07:10.696
"So that's how you swing," Ally went on, "but you also have to pay attention to the ball."

66
00:07:10.697 --> 00:07:16.848
She tossed a tennis ball up in the air and caught it with the same hand.

67
00:07:16.849 --> 00:07:22.837
"Get ready, toss the ball, shift your weight, and swing!"

68
00:07:22.838 --> 00:07:28.605
Her racket struck the ball and lobbed it a few feet in front of her.

69
00:07:28.606 --> 00:07:34.602
"Maybe Iris should just focus on her swing for now," Grace suggested.

70
00:07:34.603 --> 00:07:40.528
"Sure," Ally said. "Good idea, Grace. I need to check on Javier."

71
00:07:40.529 --> 00:07:53.161
For the rest of the morning, Grace gave Iris tips as Iris practiced her swing and hit the ball against a practice wall.

72
00:07:53.162 --> 00:08:01.813
She made some slow progress, but there was a lot to remember, and they hadn't even started to play against each other yet!

73
00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:05.644
"Lunchtime!" Ally called.

74
00:08:05.645 --> 00:08:12.062
"Phew!" Iris thought. "Practice is finally over."

75
00:08:12.063 --> 00:08:22.741
She let out a sigh and followed Grace to the shady picnic tables where they'd all left their backpacks and lunches that morning.

76
00:08:22.742 --> 00:08:25.505
Jae was standing near her stuff.

77
00:08:25.506 --> 00:08:32.975
Iris' heartbeat sped up. They were in different groups now, but maybe they could still be friends.

78
00:08:32.976 --> 00:08:37.538
Before she could call out to him, he smiled at Zoe.

79
00:08:37.539 --> 00:08:39.836
"Ready?" he asked her.

80
00:08:39.837 --> 00:08:42.878
"Ready!" Zoe replied.

81
00:08:42.878 --> 00:08:58.796
Jae glanced quickly in Iris' direction, as if he knew she was there. But instead of saying anything to her, he simply looked away.

